course: dictionary
lesson: 7151
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. «The peregrine falcon is the fastest animal, diving at over three hundred kilometres an hour.» Here a peregrine is a bird, because falcons, diving and kilometres per hour all point to an animal.
explain: «Peregrines hunt pigeons from the cathedral tower.» Ask yourself: who is doing the hunting? Birds hunt, so peregrines must be birds here. Read the words around the word, then pick the meaning that fits.
explain: Peregrine can also be an old, formal adjective meaning wandering or travelling from place to place. You will find it in older books, so if a sentence is about a traveller or a long journey, check that meaning. It is also a boy's name, so if it is a person's name, it is not a bird at all.
fact: A peregrine, or peregrine falcon, is a bird of prey that catches other birds in the air.
fact: «In a dive» means when the falcon folds its wings and drops at great speed.
fact: The peregrine falcon can dive faster than 300 kilometres per hour, which makes it the fastest animal on Earth.
fact: Peregrine falcons nest on cliffs, and also on tall buildings and cathedrals in cities.
fact: Pesticides like DDT nearly wiped out peregrines, but after they were banned, their numbers recovered.
exercise: «The peregrine falcon is the fastest animal, diving at over three hundred kilometres an hour.» What is a peregrine in this sentence? | A wandering traveller | A city tower | *A bird of prey that dives fast | A boy's name
exercise: «Peregrines hunt pigeons from the cathedral tower.» What are the peregrines in this sentence? | *Birds of prey | Cathedrals, the buildings they stand on | Towers, the places they live | Pigeons, the animals they hunt
exercise: Old book: «The peregrine traveller walked from town to town for years.» What does peregrine mean here? | A kind of cathedral | *Wandering from place to place | A very fast bird | A boy named after a bird
test: «A peregrine dives at a pigeon like a bullet.» What is the peregrine in this sentence? | A pigeon | A boy's name | A kind of cloud | *A bird of prey
test: «In a dive, the peregrine can go faster than a racing car.» What does «in a dive» mean? | Sleeping in a nest on a cliff | *When the falcon folds its wings and drops fast | Swimming under water | Hiding in a city park
exam: Jo says, «Peregrine is my friend's name, and it is also the name of a bird.» Which meaning fits Jo's friend? | *A boy's name | A cathedral tower | A wandering journey | A bird
